I walk along the path the woman said.
I come out of the market.
"Go straight," she said.
I walk straight along the main road.
The market crowd decreases.
I reach the end of the road.
"Turn right from there," she said.
I turn right.
Now I am on the big road.
I walk towards that walkway.
A nice breeze blows there.
I hear the sound of the water.
Finally, I reach the waterfront.
This is a broad walkway.
I see the open water.
There are many trees here.
People are walking here.
I look towards the water.
Kochi is very beautiful.
